# §13.4 — academic uptake is the return on this project, so make it citable from
# v1.0. A DOI is minted via the Zenodo/GitHub release integration at M8; the
# placeholder below is replaced with the concept DOI at first public release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "BuildFOAM: a desktop workbench for OpenFOAM"
abstract: >-
  A cross-platform desktop application that installs, configures and drives a
  complete OpenFOAM workflow — mesh, solve, visualise — without the user opening
  a terminal, with a built-in verification and validation workflow covering
  turbulence-model selection, grid-convergence (GCI) studies and comparison
  against experimental data.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hidayat
    family-names: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/mnhidayatmat/buildFOAM"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.0.0
keywords:
  - OpenFOAM
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - verification and validation
  - grid convergence index
  - engineering education
